```xml
<students>
    <student>
        <name>Alice</name>
        <age>22</age>
        <citizenship>US</citizenship>
        <username>alice</username>
        <password>pass123</password>
    </student>
</students>
```

---

### 📌 Usage

```go
name, age, citizenship := getStudentInfo(xmlData, "alice", "pass123")
fmt.Printf("Name: %s, Age: %s, Citizenship: %s\n", name, age, citizenship)
```

---

### ✅ Summary

This implementation ensures that:
- User input is properly escaped to prevent XPath injection.
- XML parsing is done with a secure parser that disables external entities to prevent XXE attacks.
- The code is robust and follows secure coding practices for handling XML and XPath queries.


